 34MG c  2017Li03: {+34}Mg source formed in U(p,X),E=1.4 GeV reaction           
 34MG2c  using UC{-x} target and Proton Synchrotron Booster at ISOLDE-CERN.     
 34MG3c  The Mg atoms were selectively ionized using resonance ionization laser 
 34MG4c  ion source (RILIS), accelerated to 40 keV, then A=34 ions selected     
 34MG5c  by the ISOLDE General Purpose Separator, and finally deposited on a    
 34MG6c  movable tape located at the ISOLDE Decay station. Measured E|g, I|g,   
 34MG7c  |b particles, |b-gated |g spectra, |b-gated |g|g-coin, half-life and   
 34MG8c  %|b{+-}n for {+34}Mg decay using a plastic scintillator for |b         
 34MG9c  particles, and five HPGe clover detectors for |g detection.            
